Some weeks ago somebody posted that there was a problem with
rexecd (/usr/etc/rexecd) on Ultrix 4.0! 
We have Ultrix 4.0 (rev179) installed a didn't succeed in getting
MacX working (stream came up halfway.... was the errormessage on
the Mac-side). 
The solution was posted to remove the new (4.0) rexecd with an older
one, for example from Ultrix 3.1. I did it and MacX worked fine. So 
did some other application which use rexecd! 

BUT !!!!!	There is a dangerous trap in this solution!

If you use MacX and start an 'xterm' on an Ultrix machine you 
suddenly have group-ID 0 (this is the systemgroup!!!!) Now you are
able to write to /etc for example! This should (must) not happen!!!

A college of mine phoned with DEC-Fieldservice (here in Germany/Frank-
furt a.M.) and they sent (quiet fast!) a patch!

This version is o.k.. When I log in now, i have gid=15 (users) which is
the correct one!

Good luck with other Ultrix-Problems!!!

P. Davids (davids@informatik.rwth-aachen.de)
 


